Goa packages for the Google Pixel 7

This repository holds the components for the Pixel 7 that are built with Goa, and
describes the depot they are published in. It belongs to three places:

:'repos/pixel' of the Genode tree:
  drivers, board support, and the session APIs of the drivers
:'repos/muesli' of the Genode tree:
  the MüesliOS base system
:this repository:
  applications and libraries, built with Goa against the APIs of the tree

The projects use APIs of the tree, so a Genode tree with 'repos/pixel' next to
this repository is needed to build them. Each directory with a 'version' file is
a Goa project:

:mesa26:     Mesa with the gallium drivers panfrost and softpipe, its EGL, and
             libdrm with a back end for the driver 'panthor_gpu', see its README.
:mesa26_egl: Rendering test for Mesa, without a display.
:glmark2_26: The benchmark glmark2 for this Mesa.

The other directories:

:depot: The public key and the download location of the depot user.


Depot
~~~~~

The archives are published under the depot user 'iloskutov_pixel7':

:URL:          https://iloskutov.github.io/depot-pixel
:Fingerprint:  5FE638DC1D398C533B6D09CFD14699FA22B15CAA
:Architecture: arm_v8a


Using the depot in a Genode tree
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The depot tools need the public key and the URL in a repository of the tree, Goa
needs them in the depot directory. From the Genode directory:

! U=iloskutov_pixel7
! mkdir -p repos/muesli/sculpt/depot/$U depot/$U
! cp ../goa-packages/depot/$U/* repos/muesli/sculpt/depot/$U/
! cp ../goa-packages/depot/$U/* depot/$U/

Then download archives by their versions, together with their dependencies. The
signatures are checked against the public key:

! tool/depot/download $U/bin/arm_v8a/mesa26/<version>

A run script takes such archives with 'import_from_depot'. Add the user with
these files by hand: 'goa add-depot-user' fails if the tool 'sq' is missing.


Prerequisites for building
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* Goa from 'https://github.com/iloskutov/goa', branch 'master', with 'bin/' in the
  PATH. This is upstream's 'main' with a change for hosts without
  '/etc/ca-certificates', such as Gentoo.

  ! export PATH=$PATH:<goa>/bin

* The Genode tool chain 25.05 in '/usr/local/genode/tool/25.05'.

* On the host, 'bwrap', 'expect', and 'tclsh', as Goa requires them.

* For 'mesa26', which generates sources at its import, on the host: 'meson',
  'ninja', 'flex', 'bison', the Python modules 'mako', 'yaml', and 'packaging',
  LLVM and clang, libclc with SPIR-V, SPIRV-LLVM-Translator, SPIRV-Tools, and
  SPIRV-Headers. The import runs in Goa's sandbox with the PATH '/usr/bin' and
  alike, so 'llvm-config' must be there, or in '/usr/lib/llvm/<version>/bin'.

* A Genode tree with 'repos/pixel', and a build directory as described in the
  README of 'repos/pixel'.


Configuration
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The file 'goarc' expects the Genode tree next to this repository, in
'../genode-pub'. Adapt the paths if yours is elsewhere:

! set depot_user               iloskutov_pixel7
! set versions_from_genode_dir ../genode-pub
! set depot_dir                ../genode-pub/depot
! set public_dir               ../genode-pub/public
! set arch                     arm_v8a
! set sculpt_version           26.05

The tree and this repository share one depot, so that a run script of the tree
finds the archives Goa exports. API versions come from the recipes of the tree.

Goa accepts paths outside of the project only if a privileged config allows
them. Add this line with the absolute path of the tree to '~/goarc':

! lappend allowed_paths <genode>


API archives of the tree
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The projects build against API archives that the tree creates. They need the
ports 'libc', 'stdcxx', 'zlib', 'libpng', and 'jpeg'. From the Genode directory:

! tool/ports/prepare_port libc stdcxx zlib libpng jpeg
! U=iloskutov_pixel7/api
! tool/depot/create $U/base $U/so $U/libc $U/posix $U/stdcxx $U/zlib \
!                   $U/gpu_session $U/vfs_gpu $U/gpu_panthor $U/os $U/format \
!                   $U/gui_session $U/input_session $U/framebuffer_session \
!                   $U/blit $U/libpng $U/jpeg


Building
~~~~~~~~

Run Goa from the root of this repository, where it finds the other projects
and their versions, and name the project with '-C':

! goa build -C mesa26

'mesa26' downloads the archives of Mesa and libdrm at the first build, and checks
their hashes. The directory 'mesa26/src' is generated from 'mesa26/files' and the
patches, and is not part of the repository. Change the files there, not in 'src':
Goa refuses to import over local changes in 'src'.

A library needs a file in 'symbols/'. 'goa extract-abi-symbols' creates it, review
the result and remove the line that asks for the review.


Adding a package to the depot
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

First, export the project from the root of this repository, which builds it if
needed and writes its archives into the depot of the tree:

! goa export -C mesa26
! goa export -C mesa26_egl

Export a project before building a project that uses its API. A project needs
the files 'version', 'LICENSE', 'used_apis', and 'artifacts' or 'api'. It names
APIs as '_/api/<name>'.

Second, sign the archives and their dependencies into 'public/', from the Genode
directory. This needs the secret key:

! U=iloskutov_pixel7
! tool/depot/publish $U/bin/arm_v8a/mesa26/<version> \
!                    $U/bin/arm_v8a/mesa26_egl/<version>

The tool skips archives that have a signature in 'public/' already. The content of
'public/' is what the URL above serves. The phone's download does not check the TLS
certificate of the server, trust comes from the signatures.


Versions
~~~~~~~~

Under review, versions stay as they are. Overwrite the archives of the same
version with 'goa export --depot-overwrite', and remove archives that are no
longer used from the depot. Goa ignores 'depot_overwrite' in a 'goarc' file.

A published version is final: update the 'version' file before the next change.


Signing key
~~~~~~~~~~~

Archives are signed with a key of its own for the depot user, RSA 4096 without
expiry. Create a new one only for another depot user, with a passphrase, and keep
the secret key out of all repositories:

! gpg --quick-generate-key "<name> (Genode depot <user>)" rsa4096 sign never
! gpg --list-secret-keys --with-fingerprint
! gpg --armor --export <fingerprint> > pubkey
! gpg --armor --export-secret-keys <fingerprint> > <offline backup>

Keep the backup and the revocation certificate that GPG wrote to
'~/.gnupg/openpgp-revocs.d/' offline. A lost key cannot be replaced without new
images, because the images carry the public key.


Test on the phone
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The scenarios are in 'repos/pixel/run' of the tree. They take the driver and the
base libraries from the tree, and these packages from its depot. Their headers
describe how to build and run them:

:'mesa_panfrost_pixel': rendering test with 'mesa26_egl'
:'glmark2_mali_pixel':  glmark2 on the GPU, shown on the panel

From the Genode directory, after the exports:

! repos/pixel/tool/device_test mesa_panfrost_pixel 45
! repos/pixel/tool/device_test glmark2_mali_pixel 125
